  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/cfr/text/29/778.105" rel="noopener">29 CFR §778.105 — Determining the workweek</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://www.dol.gov/agencies/whd/fact-sheets/22-flsa-hours-worked" rel="noopener">US Department of Labor — Fact Sheet #22: Hours worked under the FLSA</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/regulations/california/8-CCR-11040" rel="noopener">California Code of Regulations, Title 8, §11040 — definition of workday</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://caselaw.findlaw.com/court/ca-court-of-appeal/1573627.html" rel="noopener">Securitas Security Services USA, Inc. v. Superior Court (Cal. Ct. App. 2011)</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://www.iana.org/time-zones" rel="noopener">IANA Time Zone Database (daylight saving dates)</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://www.gov.uk/rest-breaks-work" rel="noopener">GOV.UK — Rest breaks at work</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://www.ontario.ca/document/your-guide-employment-standards-act-0/hours-work" rel="noopener">Ontario — Hours of work (rest periods)</a></li>
  </ul>
</GuideLayout>
